1
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:09,420
Bowling pins are set out in a triangle.

2
00:00:09,470 --> 00:00:14,020
The front row has 1 pin, the next row 2, then 3, and so on.

3
00:00:14,070 --> 00:00:17,600
The running totals are 1, 3, 6, 10, 15.

4
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:19,510
What are the next two totals?

5
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:23,140
Pause the video and work them out.

6
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:27,040
The totals grow by 2, then 3, then 4, then 5.

7
00:00:27,090 --> 00:00:30,700
So next we add 6, then 7: 21 and 28.

8
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:36,650
Remember: a term-to-term rule tells you how to get from one term to the next.

9
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:39,520
5, 9, 13, 17: add 4 each time.

10
00:00:39,570 --> 00:00:44,020
In a linear sequence, the terms change by the same amount each time.

11
00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:48,530
In a non-linear sequence, the change is different each time.

12
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:50,460
Look at the differences.

13
00:00:50,510 --> 00:00:55,120
For 1, 3, 6, 10, 15, the first differences are 2, 3, 4, 5.

14
00:00:55,170 --> 00:00:57,760
The second differences are all 1.

15
00:00:57,810 --> 00:01:03,050
Constant second differences mean the sequence is quadratic.

16
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:03,790
Your turn.

17
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:06,220
1 and a half, 4, 6 and a half, 9.

18
00:01:06,270 --> 00:01:09,090
Is this sequence linear, or non-linear?

19
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:12,470
Pause the video and choose.

20
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:13,370
It is linear.

21
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:16,550
It goes up by 2 and a half every time.

22
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:18,450
Rules can multiply too.

23
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:21,750
Multiply by 3 from 2 gives 2, 6, 18, 54.

24
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:25,530
Always use the previous term each time.

25
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:26,910
Here is the method.

26
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:30,590
Step 1: find the differences between terms.

27
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:33,620
Step 2: the same difference means linear.

28
00:01:33,670 --> 00:01:36,900
Changing differences mean non-linear.

29
00:01:36,950 --> 00:01:42,730
Step 3: for non-linear, look at second differences, or a multiplying rule.

30
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:46,790
Step 4: use the pattern, and check one more step.

31
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:50,670
The first term is 3, and the rule is add 3 quarters.

32
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:56,070
The terms are 3, 3 and 3 quarters, 4 and a half, 5 and a quarter.

33
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:58,960
Next term of 50, 41, 33, 26, 20?

34
00:01:59,010 --> 00:02:03,920
The differences are minus 9, minus 8, minus 7, minus 6.

35
00:02:03,970 --> 00:02:07,000
They go down by 1 each time.

36
00:02:07,050 --> 00:02:07,900
Your turn.

37
00:02:07,950 --> 00:02:11,890
What is the next term of 50, 41, 33, 26, 20?

38
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:15,290
Pause and work it out.

39
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:18,020
The next difference is minus 5.

40
00:02:18,070 --> 00:02:20,080
20 minus 5 is 15.

41
00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:24,320
A two-step rule: start at 1, double, then add 3.

42
00:02:24,370 --> 00:02:26,010
1, 5, 13, 29.

43
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:29,730
The first term is 2, and the rule is square the term.

44
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:31,480
Rosa writes the sequence.

45
00:02:31,530 --> 00:02:33,430
Which line is wrong?

46
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:34,560
Line 1 is wrong.

47
00:02:34,610 --> 00:02:37,240
She squared the first term every time.

48
00:02:37,290 --> 00:02:40,550
Each term comes from the previous term.

49
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:43,400
2, 4, 16, 256.

50
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:46,910
Bacteria can split in two every 20 minutes.

51
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:52,280
1, 2, 4, 8, 16: a non-linear sequence that grows very fast.

52
00:02:52,330 --> 00:02:53,740
One last question.

53
00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:54,800
3, 6, 12, 24.

54
00:02:54,850 --> 00:02:57,820
Is it non-linear, times 2, or linear?

55
00:02:57,870 --> 00:03:01,420
Pause the video and choose.

56
00:03:01,470 --> 00:03:03,670
The differences are 3, 6, 12.

57
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:06,230
They change, so it is non-linear.

58
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:08,330
The rule is times 2.

59
00:03:08,380 --> 00:03:12,990
To remember: linear sequences have a constant difference.

60
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:18,470
Non-linear sequences have changing differences, or a multiplying rule.

61
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:22,080
Constant second differences mean quadratic.

62
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:24,640
Rules act on the previous term.

63
00:03:24,690 --> 00:03:29,830
Great work! Now practise lesson 9.1 on Camday.
